This test case looks at accuracy of strain rate, stress, and velocity computations.

The problem consists of assigning u,v components of velocity, computing strain
rate and stress. The MP velocity is initialized so that each component is
a spherical harmonic.  The MP velocity is reconstructed on the mesh.  Strain
rate is computed from the mesh velocity field.  MPM computes strains using the
mpm algorithm: differentiate Wachspress basis functions in the tangent plane to
get a strain rate for each material point.

The constitutive model for stress is 'linear'.  So each material point has a stress equal to the strain rate.
-mpmvar takes material point stress to mesh vertices (in preparation for the variational stress divergence)
-mpmweak takes material point stress to mesh cell centers (in preparatation for the weak stress divergence)
-mpm has stress only at material points (used in the mpm stress divergence)

velocity_map plots the vertex values of velocity reconstructed from the MP values, and the error for one mesh size.
velocity_scaling plots the error in the reconstructed velocity as a function of grid resolution.

strain_map plots the analytical solution for the strain on a mesh and a scatter plot of MPs for one mesh
resolution. The error is also plotted.
strain_scaling plots the norm of the error in each strain component.

stess_scaling plots the norm of the error in each stress component as a function of mesh resolution for
each method.
stress_map plots the analytical solution for stress on a mesh and a scatter plot of MPs for one mesh resolution.
The error is also plotted.
